> Do they still stack when (individually) named?

Yes they do.  I was surprised to discover this,
but I now have significant experience with it.
At this point, if I have a #named non-cursed dagger
in my inventory and find an altar, I try to remember
NOT to drop it on there, because if it's officially
identified as uncursed new daggers I pick up
will no longer stack with it.

Of course, if you have two daggers with different
names, then they won't stack.  But an unnamed
item will stack with a #named one if its properties
are otherwise the same (beatitude and so forth).
For most types of items this is not really very
significant, but I've found it to be very useful with
daggers in particular.


